  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🪄 Wand Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Wood, core, length and temper, or a name of its own: Thornwhisper, a hawthorn wand with a phoenix feather core."
    },
    "intro": "Some wands are tools and some are characters. This **wand name generator** does both: a full wand-maker's description (wood, length, core and flexibility, in the style made famous by Ollivander), a named wand with a story, or a magic item in the D&amp;D style, like the <em>Wand of Lingering Frost</em>.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Wood, core, length and flexibility",
        "content": "<p>In Harry Potter, Ollivander describes every wand the same way. Harry's is holly and phoenix feather, eleven inches, nice and supple; Hermione's is vine. Ollivander only uses three cores: phoenix feather, dragon heartstring and unicorn hair. Other wand-makers use other things, so the generator adds a few more, like kelpie mane and thestral tail hair.</p><ul><li><strong>Length</strong> runs from about 9 to 14 inches.</li><li><strong>Flexibility</strong> says something about the owner: <em>unyielding</em> for the stubborn, <em>supple</em> for the adaptable, <em>brittle</em> for a wand that won't last.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "What the woods mean",
        "content": "<p>Wand woods borrow from the folklore of trees:</p><ul><li><strong>Rowan</strong> was planted by doors in Britain to keep witches and <a href=\"fairy-name-generator.html\">fairies</a> out: a protective wood.</li><li><strong>Hazel</strong> is the dowser's wood, used to find water underground.</li><li><strong>Yew</strong> grows in churchyards and lives for thousands of years, linked with death and rebirth. Voldemort's wand is yew.</li><li><strong>Elder</strong> was thought unlucky to burn or cut, which suits the most dangerous wand in the books.</li><li><strong>Blackthorn</strong> and <strong>hawthorn</strong> are hedgerow woods of witches and fairies; <strong>holly</strong> stays green all winter.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Wands in games",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>D&amp;D</strong> wands are magic items named for what they do: the Wand of Magic Missiles, the Wand of Fireballs. The \"Wand of…\" format gives you new ones to use as treasure.</li><li><strong>Hogwarts Legacy</strong> lets you choose wood, core, length and flexibility for your character's wand, exactly the details the wand-maker format gives you.</li><li><strong>A named wand</strong> is for something rarer: an heirloom, a stolen wand, a wand that chose its owner.</li></ul><p>For something taller, try the <a href=\"staff-name-generator.html\">Staff Name Generator</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "What are the three wand cores in Harry Potter?",
        "answer": "Ollivander uses phoenix feather, dragon heartstring and unicorn hair. Other wand-makers in the books use other cores; Fleur Delacour's wand contains a Veela hair."
      },
      {
        "question": "What wand wood should I choose?",
        "answer": "Pick one whose folklore fits your character: rowan for protection, hazel for finding things, yew for something old and deathly, holly for hope in dark times."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can I use these for D&D or my own story?",
